      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-147416",
      ":question/problem": "The joint probability mass function $f(x, y)$ for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given below.\n\n| $f$ | $Y = 0$ | $Y = 1$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| $X = 0$ | $0.28$ | $0.12$ |\n| $X = 1$ | $0.42$ | $0.18$ |\n\nCalculate the covariance of $X$ and $Y$.\n\n*Hint: It can be shown that $P(X = x, Y = y) = P(X = x) \\cdot P(Y = y)$ for all possible values of $x$ and $y$.*\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."
